[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Futex
REQ_PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-37-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Futex
TITLE: Pending on a futex with a changed value
STATEMENT: >>>
When a thread attempts to pend on a futex and the futex value differs from the expected
value, the Zephyr RTOS shall return immediately with an error indicating the futex value
changed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-36

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Futex
TITLE: Waking threads pending on a futex
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to wake either the highest-priority thread or all threads pending on a futex.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-36

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Futex
TITLE: Futex operation from user mode
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall allow user mode threads to operate on a futex located in memory
they can access.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-36

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Futex
TITLE: Pending on a futex with a matching value
STATEMENT: >>>
When a thread attempts to pend on a futex and the futex value matches the expected
value, the Zephyr RTOS shall block the thread until the futex is woken or the specified
timeout elapses.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-36

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-37-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Futex
TITLE: Futex access control
STATEMENT: >>>
If a futex operation refers to memory the calling thread cannot access, then the Zephyr
RTOS shall reject the operation with an error indicating the access is denied.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-36
